WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.850
Quick test. Which of these is AI: a calculator, a spam filter, autocomplete, or an alarm clock?

2
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:14.183
A calculator follows fixed rules that a person wrote. Two plus two is four, every single time.

3
00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:22.192
A spam filter is different. It learned from millions of emails that people marked as spam, and it keeps adjusting.

4
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:32.667
So here is the test: did the system learn its behavior from examples? Spam filter and autocomplete, yes. Calculator and alarm clock, no.

5
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:42.108
Every AI you use today is narrow AI. It is built for one kind of task. A model that writes fluent paragraphs cannot drive a car.

6
00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:51.467
General AI, one system that could learn any task the way people do, is still a research goal. It is not what is on your phone.

7
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:59.383
So when a headline says an app understands everything, ask: what one task did it learn, and from what examples?

8
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:06.992
Let's mark up the definition. Fixed rules on one side, learning from examples on the other.

9
00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:09.692
Here is the test to remember.

10
00:01:10.142 --> 00:01:15.792
And the name for the tools you use today: narrow AI, built for one kind of task.
